<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krasnodar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yekaterinodar, Ekaterinodar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krasnodar is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on the Kuban River and the capital of Krasnodar Krai. It was founded in 1793 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> as a fort named Yekaterinodar, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a>, and became the capital of the Kuban Cossack Host. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a> it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Kuban Rada</a> and changed hands repeatedly, and it was renamed Krasnodar in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krasnodar.jpg" alt="Krasnodar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maska999 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krasnodar_teatr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
